  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Saturday) \nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Sat Jul 18 2026\n\nThe overall trend of warmer and drier remains the forecast with\nany storm coverage likely more isolated by Sunday afternoon.\nDewpoint trends will become the more uncertain forecast element\nregarding excessive heat conditions. It still appears likely that\nheat advisories will be needed for portions of the area possibly\nby Sunday and more likely by Monday. \n\nSfc winds gradually veer both Monday and Tuesday afternoon\nbecoming west of south for most the area with the pre frontal\nthermal axis aligned across the region by Tuesday afternoon. Both\ndays hold potential for triple digit heat for portions of the\nforecast area, and pending dewpoint trends, excessive heat\nwarnings may be needed by Tuesday afternoon. \n\nThe weak cold front remains in the forecast to arrive Tuesday \nnight into early Wednesday. The frontal zone is likely to become\noriented NW to SE in or near the forecast area on the periphery of\nthe upper level ridge. Any sustained cooling associated with the\nfront will largely depend on any more widespread precip developing\nwithin the frontal corridor as the post frontal airmass will be\nlacking for a robust airmass change. There remains considerable\nuncertainty in these details for the mid to late week forecast.",
